  "text": "One of the richest everyday lignan sources. Lignans are plant compounds that gut bacteria can turn into enterolignans, giving flax a named-compound story beyond the visible nutrient rows. Grinds into an egg-free baking binder. Mix ground flax with water and it forms a gel that can help bind pancakes, muffins, and other bakes. Cheap and shelf-stable whole. The intact seeds keep well and are easy to add to porridge, yoghurt, or dough without a full recipe.",
